def keep_reason(key,label):
 if key=='fly':return 'Usable adult-fly group symbol. The label/prose supplies species and larval damage; not a species-identification image.'
 if key=='beetle':return 'Usable beetle-family cue, including weevils; species-specific jumping/notches are supplied by text.'
 if key=='caterpillar':return 'Shows the damaging larval stage; appropriate even when the condition is named for the moth.'
 if key=='slug':return 'Clear representative slug; combined snail labels remain explicit in text.'
 if key=='bird':return 'Pigeon is a useful representative garden-bird cue; not a claim that every bird mentioned is a pigeon.'
 if key=='bolting':return 'Clear flowering-stalk cue. Generic host shape is acceptable for the same bolting process, including alliums.'
 if key=='blossom_drop':return 'Usable general blossom/fruit-set failure cue for this flowering crop; not a diagnosis of the cause.'
 if key=='forked_root':return 'Clearly depicts forking. Carrot-shaped subject is an acceptable shared root-deformity cue on this crop.'
 if key=='splitting':return 'Clear open split in a storage root; a round-root silhouette is a usable generic root-splitting cue on carrot.'
 if key=='weed':return 'Taprooted perennial weed is a general weed cue; text retains couch/bindweed distinctions.'
 if key=='deficiency':return 'Interveinal leaf marking is relevant to the described nutrient symptom; the image alone does not diagnose manganese deficiency.'
 return 'Named subject or main symptom is clearly represented; retain the written label for identification.'
